Pull Up to 7-Eleven in Forza Horizon 6
Every good drive has a convenience store stop along the way somewhere. Starting today, that stop becomes possible for a limited time inside Forza Horizon 6 . XBOX and 7-Eleven, Inc. are teaming up on the new Horizon Meets update – as well as releasing a merch collection and an in-store offer across the US and Canada.&nbsp;
If you&#8217;re new to the Evolving World, it&#8217;s how Forza Horizon 6 keeps changing under your tires. For the Horizon Meets update, Playground Games is dropping a storefront inspired by 7-Eleven into the world, featuring a themed Car Meet. Head to the game’s Nangan region, bring friends, park the rides you&#8217;ve made, and download the car liveries and tuning setups on display from other players.&nbsp;
Beyond the store itself, you can rep 7-Eleven in Forza Horizon 6’s Japan in a number of new ways:&nbsp;
Egg Salad Sandwich Collectible : Smash 20 Egg Salad Sandwich Collectibles (find them near the 7-Eleven Evolving World Car Meet) during Autumn and earn Points completion towards the Festival Playlist, as well as a new Forza LINK reward.
There’s far more coming in the Horizon Meets update – check out Forza.net for all the details.&nbsp;
The real-life7-Eleven x Forza Horizon 6 merch drop arrives October 8, exclusively on 7Collection.com with hoodies, shirts, hats, and accessories featuring Toyota cars from the game in original Japanese-inspired art styles.
The Horizon Meets update is available to download now, with the Festival Playlist and Evolving World content rolling out today. Grab a Slurpee drink, pick up an XBOX Gift Card, and we&#8217;ll see you in the parking lot.&nbsp;&nbsp;
